**Title: Valid Parentheses Checker**

**Main Goal:** This code determines whether a given string of brackets (`()`, `{}`, `[]`) is **valid** — meaning every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket of the same type and they are correctly nested.

**How it works (deobfuscated):**

```javascript
function isValidParentheses(s) {
    const stack = [];
    const map = { '(': ')', '{': '}', '[': ']' };

    for (const char of s) {
        if (map[char]) {
            // If it's an opening bracket, push it onto the stack
            stack.push(char);
        } else {
            // If it's a closing bracket, check if it matches the last opening bracket
            if (stack.length === 0 || map[stack.pop()] !== char) {
                return false;
            }
        }
    }
    // Valid only if all opening brackets have been matched (stack is empty)
    return stack.length === 0;
}
```

